{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Moreover the sun.</b> It returns to the stillborn, and he said: Behold the stillborn, who did not see the light of the world and did not know anything — rest was his, for he did not toil in the affairs of the world. But this man of wealth — he saw the light of the world and did know, yet he had no rest, only toil without reward and no pleasure in both worlds."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The heading 'גם שמש' (also Qohelet 6:5) may reflect a variant verse division; the comment's content concerns the contrast beginning at 6:3–4."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:53.314685781Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}